{"name":"Steamy Dumpling","hex":"#eae9b4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steamy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Warm and humid; full of steam.","Resembling or characteristic of steam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steamy"},{"term":"dumpling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball of dough that is cooked and may have a filling and/or additional ingredients in the dough. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n Specifically, a ball of dough used in stews and other sauced dishes; a thick noodle.\n Specifically, a food composed of a dough wrapper around a filling.","Specifically, a ball of dough used in stews and other sauced dishes; a thick noodle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumpling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steam","blocks":[{"text":"Steam is water vapor, often mixed with air and/or an aerosol of liquid water droplets. This may occur by evaporation or by boiling, where heat is applied until water reaches the enthalpy of vaporization. Superheated or saturated steam is invisible; however, wet steam, a visible mist or aerosol of water droplets, is often referred to as \"steam\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg/330px-Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam","wikidata":"Q3251738"},{"title":"Dumpling","blocks":[{"text":"Dumplings are a broad class of dishes that consist of pieces of cooked dough, often wrapped around a filling. The dough can be based on bread, wheat or other flours, or potatoes, and it may be filled with meat, fish, tofu, cheese, vegetables, or a combination. Dumplings may be prepared using a variety of cooking methods and are found in many world cuisines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/HK_SYP_%E8%A5%BF%E7%87%9F%E7%9B%A4_Sai_Ying_Pun_Kwan_Yick_Building_%E5%90%8D%E6%98%9F%E6%B5%B7%E9%AE%AE%E9%85%92%E5%AE%B6_Star_Seafood_Restaurant_food_%E5%90%9E%E9%BA%B5_Wonton_dim_sum_October_2020_SS2_01.jpg/330px-HK_SYP_%E8%A5%BF%E7%87%9F%E7%9B%A4_Sai_Ying_Pun_Kwan_Yick_Building_%E5%90%8D%E6%98%9F%E6%B5%B7%E9%AE%AE%E9%85%92%E5%AE%B6_Star_Seafood_Restaurant_food_%E5%90%9E%E9%BA%B5_Wonton_dim_sum_October_2020_SS2_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dumpling","wikidata":"Q1854639"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/500px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/1280px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/500px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boiling water creating steam in an electric kettle ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoilingkettle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg/500px-Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg/500px-Dampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fireless steam locomotive. Despite the resemblance to a boiler, note the lack of a chimney and also how the cylinders are at the cab end, not the chimney end.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADampfspeicherlok_Genthin_Henkel_Werk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Pelmeni_Russian.jpg/500px-